1  | ∃x (P(x) ∧ (Q(x) ∨ (x=m(x))))
2  | ∀x (Q(x) → P(m(x)))
   |----
3  | | [a] P(a) ∧ (Q(a) ∨ (a=m(a)))
   | |----
4  | | P(a)                                 ∧ Elim: 3
5  | | Q(a) ∨ (a=m(a))                      ∧ Elim: 3
6  | | | Q(a)
   | | |----
7  | | | Q(a) → P(m(a))                     ∀ Elim: 2
8  | | | P(m(a))                            → Elim: 7,6
9  | | | P(a) ∧ P(m(a))                     ∧ Intro: 4, 8
   | |
10 | | | a=m(a)
   | | |----
11 | | | P(m(a))                            = Elim: 4, 10
12 | | | P(a) ∧ P(m(a))                     ∧ Intro: 4, 11
13 | | P(a) ∧ P(m(a))                       ∨ Elim: 5, 6-9, 10-12
14 | | ∃x (P(x) ∧ P(m(x)))                  ∃ Intro: 13
15 | ∃x (P(x) ∧ P(m(x)))                    ∃ Elim: 1, 3-14
